# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large binaries live in Google Cloud Storage, not here. See README §Artifacts.
# GitHub rejects files over 100 MB and degrades badly past ~1 GB of history, and
# once a big file is committed it stays in the history even after deletion.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
midi_results/weights/
deim_results/weights/
DEIMv2checkpoints/
models/
*.pt
*.pth
*.mlpackage/
*.mlmodel
*.onnx

# Environments and third-party source
.venv*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# upstream DEIMv2 clone; pinned by commit in the README instead
# (note: gitignore has no trailing comments -- they become part of the pattern)
deim_local/

# Upload staging / archives — regenerable
kaggle/upload/
vast/
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Machine-local caches
*.cache
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERSONAL DATA — photographs of a person's hands.
# Excluded by default. Publishing images of an identifiable person is a decision
# the subject makes deliberately, not one a .gitignore should make silently.
# To publish them, delete these lines AND add a LICENSE/consent note saying so.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
photov2/
photov2_annotate/
addedphoto/
needs_fixing/
qa_overlays/
overlays/
photos/
masks/
data/pool/hbb/images/
data/pool/obb/images/
deim_data/

# The source photographs show the subject's FACE, not only their hands: they are
# webcam-style frames with the person and their home interior in shot. Treat every
# image derived from them as identifiable personal data.
# Belt and braces -- catch stray debug montages and overlays wherever they sit:
_label_check.jpg
*_overlay*.jpg
*_qa*.jpg
**/photo*/**
*.JPG
*.jpeg
*.HEIC

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated at runtime, and full of absolute local paths.
# train_yolo.py rebuilds the split manifests from folds.json on whatever machine
# it runs on, precisely because a stale manifest makes ultralytics report
# "0 images found" and train on nothing without raising. Shipping them would be
# actively harmful as well as leaking a home directory into a public repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/splits/fold*/
data/splits/hbb/
data/splits/obb/
data/splits/*.txt
data/yolo/
deim_configs/
